NEW — the ONE place a mount prefix is written down in this repo. Mirrors `page-objects/base/sets.ts` in SIBLING-SET-PLAN §10.3.

```ts
export const SET_BASES = {
  liveAnimals: '/live-animals',
  plantProducts: '/plant-products',
} as const;

export type SetBase = (typeof SET_BASES)[keyof typeof SET_BASES];
```

Why a constant map and not a literal at each call site: the frontend derives its mount mechanically as `'/' + setId` (SIBLING-SET-PLAN §4.3) and pins that with a boot tripwire (pp-058). This repo cannot see that tripwire, so it needs exactly one written-down copy of the fact; a prefix scattered across 30 specs is the drift the R7 symmetry decision exists to prevent. Do NOT put the prefix in a base URL — see the config row below.

plantProducts is declared NOW even though nothing uses it until pp-062, so pp-060's move does not have to touch this file again.
